TIHabModuleTemplate.displayName.HabModuleHimalazianGeneLab=Himalazian Gene-Lab
TIHabModuleTemplate.description.HabModuleHimalazianGeneLab=Secret biolabs that include containment facilities and genetic engineering rapid prototyping centers for the Emperor's great work.

TIHabModuleTemplate.displayName.TerraMiningComplex=Terrestrial Mining Complex
TIHabModuleTemplate.description.TerraMiningComplex=An extensive complex of mines and refineries supported by a large catapult that extracts, processes and delivers Terra's raw materials to other space bodies.
TIHabModuleTemplate.displayName.HabModuleHiveSkeleton=Hive Skeleton (Decayed)
TIHabModuleTemplate.description.HabModuleHiveSkeleton=The hive skeleton represents the architectural supports, integrity fields, and gridworks to hold up the weight of other hive sections. If it were ever to collapse, all the denizens of the hive would surely perish. Poor stuructural integrity may result in sections of the hive collapsing onto lower ones, known as hivequakes. It also protects against external environmental hazards, such as radstorms. This Hive's internal structures are worn with age and lack of maintenance.
TIHabModuleTemplate.displayName.HabModuleHiveSkeletonRestored=Hive Skeleton (Restored)
TIHabModuleTemplate.description.HabModuleHiveSkeletonRestored=The hive skeleton represents the architectural supports, integrity fields, and gridworks to hold up the weight of other hive sections. If it were ever to collapse, all the denizens of the hive would surely perish. Poor stuructural integrity may result in sections of the hive collapsing onto lower ones, known as hivequakes. It also protects against external environmental hazards, such as radstorms. This Hive's internal structures have been repaired with the aid of the OCS templates, and the integrity fields have been empowered with OCS configurations.
TIHabModuleTemplate.displayName.HabModuleHiveUnderhive=Underhive
TIHabModuleTemplate.description.HabModuleHiveUnderhive=The Underhive is a region of a hive city where the poorest of the poor and those citizens of the hive city who have been exiled for committing crimes or for political reasons live.
TIHabModuleTemplate.displayName.HabModuleHiveMine=Lower Hive Recycling Complex (Decayed)
TIHabModuleTemplate.description.HabModuleHiveMine=A hive does not have any normal mineral or mining output, having long ago exhausted whatever mineral veins that might have existed. Instead, these complexes represent the many air, water, and food reclamation centers that recyle waste products into useful materials. These complexes are barely keeping up with the demands of millions of hive dwellers, with long waste backlogs and patchwork jury-rigging.
TIHabModuleTemplate.displayName.HabModuleHiveMineRestored=Lower Hive Recycling Complex (Restored)
TIHabModuleTemplate.description.HabModuleHiveMineRestored=A hive does not have any normal mineral or mining output, having long ago exhausted whatever mineral veins that might have existed. Instead, these complexes represent the many air, water, and food reclamation centers that recyle waste products into useful materials. These complexes have been restored with the arcological knowledge contained in the OCS templates.

TIHabModuleTemplate.displayName.HabModuleHiveHeavyFusionReactors=Lower Hive Fusion Reactors (Decayed)
TIHabModuleTemplate.description.HabModuleHiveHeavyFusionReactors=Home to the massive fusion plasma generators that provide the entire hive city's power production, using pooly understood techno-methods. These have degraded far from their original specifications, and only continue to function due to patchwork jury-rigging. 
TIHabModuleTemplate.displayName.HabModuleHiveHeavyFusionReactorsRestored=Lower Hive Fusion Reactors (Restored)
TIHabModuleTemplate.description.HabModuleHiveHeavyFusionReactorsRestored=Home to the massive fusion plasma generators that provide the entire hive city's power production. These have been restored to their original OCS specifications. 
TIHabModuleTemplate.displayName.HabModuleHiveHabBlock=Lower Hive Hab-Blocks (Decayed)
TIHabModuleTemplate.description.HabModuleHiveHabBlock=Home to many floors of habitation zones, with row after row of individual shelters, providing the average hive denizen a moderate level of comfort and safety for millions of hive-dwellers. Many floors are organized into neighborhoods that contain their own self-sufficient economies that provide for local needs, but nowhere near enough for the entire hive. These hab-blocks have degraded over the millenia into barely habitable slum-zones. 
TIHabModuleTemplate.displayName.HabModuleHiveHabBlockRestored=Lower Hive Hab-Blocks (Restored)
TIHabModuleTemplate.description.HabModuleHiveHabBlockRestored=Home to many floors of habitation zones, with row after row of individual shelters, providing the average hive denizen a moderate level of comfort and safety for millions of hive-dwellers. Many floors are organized into neighborhoods that contain their own self-sufficient economies that provide for local needs, but nowhere near enough for the entire hive. These hab blocks have been restored with the aid of the OCS templates, providing moderately better living conditions.
TIHabModuleTemplate.displayName.HabModuleHiveAgricultureComplex=Lower Hive Agriculture Complex
TIHabModuleTemplate.description.HabModuleHiveAgricultureComplex=Home to the massive tanks of vat-grown algae and protein reprocessers that provide the majority of the hive city's food production, using pooly understood techno-methods. 
TIHabModuleTemplate.displayName.HabModuleHiveManufactorum=Lower Hive Manufactorum
TIHabModuleTemplate.description.HabModuleHiveManufactorum=Home to the massive factories and manfuactorums that produce all of the everyday neccessities for the hive's populace, using pooly understood techno-methods. 


TIHabModuleTemplate.displayName.HabModuleHiveAdministrationCenter=Upper Hive Administration Center (Corrupt)
TIHabModuleTemplate.description.HabModuleHiveAdministrationCenter=Home to the bureaucrats who administer the hive on a day-to-day basis, top manufactorum managers and various important people connected to the Hive's political and economic nobility live. Corruption runs rampant, as many hive noble families have taken the reins of industy to serve their own petty feuds, weakening the overall economy of the hive. 
TIHabModuleTemplate.displayName.HabModuleHiveGarrisonTechnoBarbarian=Hive Garrison (Techno-Barbarians)
TIHabModuleTemplate.description.HabModuleHiveGarrisonTechnoBarbarian=Home to the local garrison, who will defend the hive against enemy invasion, but whose primary concern is the suppression of worker insurrections and repelling incursion of mutants and other horrors from the Underhive. This garrison consists of groups of Techno-Barbarians under the command of the local warlord, who in turn may swear allegiance to a larger polity in the region.

TIHabModuleTemplate.displayName.HabModuleHiveResearchUniversity=Hive Spire Research Center
TIHabModuleTemplate.description.HabModuleHiveResearchUniversity=The hive city's Spires are the furthest from the horrors of the lower levels and as such are the most luxuriously outfitted, serving as the homes of the wealthiest and most powerful people in the city, including the planetary Imperial nobility, the wealthiest merchants, industrial barons and any visitors of importance from off-world. This spire is dedicated to the preservation of what little knowledge is left to help maintain the hive's systems.
TIHabModuleTemplate.displayName.HabModuleHiveSpaceport=Hive Spire Spaceport (Decayed)
TIHabModuleTemplate.description.HabModuleHiveSpaceport=The spaceport on this spire serves as a link to other hive cities and the wider Solar system. The docking fees and taxes on incoming goods provide a nice income, while the local security forces help with any local insurrections. This spaceport has seen better days, with many of the docking bays and hangars filled with the decaying metal hulks of ancient spaceships.  
TIHabModuleTemplate.displayName.HabModuleHiveNobleSpire=Noble's Spire (Decadent)
TIHabModuleTemplate.description.HabModuleHiveNobleSpire=The Spires provide plentiful food, power and the most advanced medical care available. Every family in the Spires has access to what is essentially the hive city equivalent of a mansion or villa. But in some ways the Spires are even more dangerous than the Underhive due to the political machinations that are hatched and carried out there. In the Underhive you may be murdered for a piece of bread, but in the Spires your enemies may seek to steal your very soul. The noble families of these spires are used to having their way for millenia, and have fallen into decadent displays of wealth and influence.
TIHabModuleTemplate.displayName.HabModuleHiveSpaceDefencesSpire=Spire Anti-Space Defences (Decayed)
TIHabModuleTemplate.description.HabModuleHiveSpaceDefencesSpire=This section of the hive represents the various anti-space turrets and emplacements that bristle along the ouside edges of the Hive's spires. These emplacements have degraded severely over the millenia, and are able to shoot down medium-sized aerospace craft and debris falling from Terran orbit, but little else. 




TIHabModuleTemplate.displayName.HabModuleForgeSkeleton=Forge Skeleton
TIHabModuleTemplate.description.HabModuleForgeSkeleton=The forge skeleton represents the architectural supports, integrity fields, and gridworks to hold up the weight of other forge sections. If it were ever to collapse, all the denizens of the forge would surely perish. It also protects against external environmental hazards, such as radstorms.
TIHabModuleTemplate.displayName.HabModuleForgeMine=Forge Subterranean Mining Tunnels
TIHabModuleTemplate.description.HabModuleForgeMine=The forge extends tendrils of mining shafts and geosampling probes to discover new mineral veins in the never-ending demand for mineral resources to feed the manufactorums. 
TIHabModuleTemplate.displayName.HabModuleForgeHeavyFusionReactors=Forge Fusion Reactors
TIHabModuleTemplate.description.HabModuleForgeHeavyFusionReactors=Home to the massive fusion plasma generators that provide the entire forge's power production.
TIHabModuleTemplate.displayName.HabModuleForgeMenialQuarters=Forge Menial Living Quarters
TIHabModuleTemplate.description.HabModuleForgeMenialQuarters=Home to many floors of habitation zones, with row after row of individual shelters, providing the average forge denizen a minimum level of comfort and safety for millions of forge menials. Many floors are organized into neighborhoods that contain their own self-sufficient economies that provide for local needs, but nowhere near enough for the entire forge. 
TIHabModuleTemplate.displayName.HabModuleForgeManufactorum=Forge Manufactorum (Various)
TIHabModuleTemplate.description.HabModuleForgeManufactorum=Home to the massive factories and manfuactorums that produce all of the everyday neccessities for the forge's populace. This manufactorum produces a wide variety of goods.
TIHabModuleTemplate.displayName.HabModuleForgeGarrisonSkitarii=Forge Garrison (Skitarii)
TIHabModuleTemplate.description.HabModuleForgeGarrisonSkitarii=Home to the local garrison, who will defend the forge against enemy invasion, but whose primary concern is the suppression of worker insurrections. This garrison consists of groups of Skitarii, augmented humans armed with the best standardized equipment the forge has to offer.
TIHabModuleTemplate.displayName.HabModuleForgeAdministrationCenter=Forge Administration Center 
TIHabModuleTemplate.description.HabModuleForgeAdministrationCenter=Home to the bureaucrats who administer the forge on a day-to-day basis, top manufactorum managers and various important people connected to the Forges's political and economic nobility live. 
TIHabModuleTemplate.displayName.HabModuleForgeSpaceport=Forge Spaceport 
TIHabModuleTemplate.description.HabModuleForgeSpaceport=The spaceport for this forge serves as a link to other forges and the wider Solar system. The docking fees and taxes on incoming goods provide a nice income, while the local security forces help with any local insurrections. 
TIHabModuleTemplate.displayName.HabModuleForgeForgeMasterLabMagosBiologis=Forge Master's Labs (Magos Biologis)
TIHabModuleTemplate.description.HabModuleForgeForgeMasterLabMagosBiologis=These are the personal research labs, armories, and data archives of the Forge Master. These appear to belong to a Magos Bioogis, specialzing in the life sciences.
TIHabModuleTemplate.displayName.HabModuleForgeSpaceDefences=Forge Anti-Space Defences
TIHabModuleTemplate.description.HabModuleForgeSpaceDefences=This section of the forge represents the various anti-space turrets and emplacements that bristle along the ouside edges of the Forge. 

TIHabModuleTemplate.displayName.HabModuleForgeTempleofAllKnowledge=Temple of All Knowledge
TIHabModuleTemplate.description.HabModuleForgeTempleofAllKnowledge=The Temple of All Knowledge is a sacred site of the Adeptus Mechanicus. Its creation came shortly after the establishment of the Cult Mechanicus in the Age of Strife and the newly formed Tech-Priests scoured the surface of ruined Mars, with any technology being enshrined within this temple. Its plasteel shell contains shining pistons that hold a vaulted roof which stands almost a mile above them. The construction of the pistons allows them to raise or lower the roof to allow adherents to change the acoustic properties within the temple, which allows worshipers to better attenuate their hymms as they sing their praise to the Machine God. Any STC fragments that are recovered eventually wind up here to be venerated as a fragment of the Ommnisiah's knowledge. 


TIHabModuleTemplate.displayName.HabModuleSentinelComplex=Decrepit Orbit-to-Surface Weapons Complex  (Vault)
TIHabModuleTemplate.description.HabModuleSentinelComplex=A crumbling, yet massive, arsenal of orbit-to-surface weaponry, perhaps intended to obliterate threats on the surface.



TIMiningProfileTemplate.displayName.TerraHiveMine=Terran Hive
TIMiningProfileTemplate.description.TerraHiveMine=Hive Waste Recycling
TIMiningProfileTemplate.displayName.TerraMountainMine=Terran Mountain Veins
TIMiningProfileTemplate.description.TerraMountainMine=Underground veins and ice formation







