TIProjectTemplate.displayName.Project_VaultRewardHimalazianGeneLabRejuv=Himalazian Rejuv Treatment
TIProjectTemplate.summary.Project_VaultRewardHimalazianGeneLabRejuv=Taken from the Himalazian Gene-labs, molecular manipulation technologies allow nanorobots to repair damage to human DNA strands.
TIProjectTemplate.description.Project_VaultRewardHimalazianGeneLabRejuv=This experimental rejuvenant treatment dates from the Dark Age of Technology. It never saw mass introduction, as the treatment was deemed too expensive at the time for mass use. However, the steroidal elixirs used in the treatment are replicable using currently available technology. This would aid in improving the lifespans of loyal agents of the Imperium, extending their usefulness. 
TIProjectTemplate.displayName.Project_VaultRewardUnderhiveOlympusAdminArchive=OCS Administrative Archive
TIProjectTemplate.summary.Project_VaultRewardUnderhiveOlympusAdminArchive=This data-archive was retrieved from an ancient vault deep in the Underhive of a Terran Hive city.
TIProjectTemplate.description.Project_VaultRewardUnderhiveOlympusAdminArchive=The Archive retrieved by our agents reveals quite a bit about this ancient organization from the Dark Age of Technology. The earliest date in the Archive places the founding of the Olympus Construction Systems, LLC. corporation, as it was known at the time, around 316.M16. Over the millenia, it went through many mergers and aquisitions, suffered several corporate takeovers, and wen through hundreds of boom and bust cycles. However, despite what the current owners, corporate oversight board, or hostile acquisitions teams did to the main company, it never changed its corporate motto from "Building towards the Heaveans!". In 523.M18 they were invited to participate in the early stage of the Standard Template Construct project for their expertise in arcology construction. This was a huge success for the comapny, and from then on they were far more resistant to hostile aquisistions and economic depressions, and maintained an iron-clad monopoly on the arcology construction industry. Every colony ship of note needed an STC, and OCS's licensing fees kept them in the black. The Archive abruply ends sometime in 042.M23. We can only speculate as to why.<br/><br/>The archive is a treasure trove of information that may lead in developments in administrative and business methods.
TIProjectTemplate.displayName.Project_VaultRewardUnderhiveOlympusAdminArchiveResearchBusinessMethods=OCS Business Models
TIProjectTemplate.summary.Project_VaultRewardUnderhiveOlympusAdminArchiveResearchBusinessMethods=By learning from the millenia of OCS business and operations history detailed in the OCS archive, we can improve our own economic endeavours
TIProjectTemplate.description.Project_VaultRewardUnderhiveOlympusAdminArchiveResearchBusinessMethods=Olympus Construction Systems, LLC. has existed for millenia. It went through many mergers and aquisitions, suffered several corporate takeovers, and wen through hundreds of boom and bust cycles. However, despite what the current owners, corporate oversight board, or hostile acquisitions teams did to the main company, it never changed its corporate motto from "Building Towards the Heaveans!".<br/><br/>In its darkest hours, the employees of the company never lost hope. And we should follow their example.
TIProjectTemplate.displayName.Project_VaultRewardUnderhiveOlympusAdminArchiveResearchConstructionMethods=OCS Construction Logisitics
TIProjectTemplate.summary.Project_VaultRewardUnderhiveOlympusAdminArchiveResearchConstructionMethods=By learning from the millenia of OCS business and operations history detailed in the OCS archive, we can improve our own construction processes
TIProjectTemplate.description.Project_VaultRewardUnderhiveOlympusAdminArchiveResearchConstructionMethods=Olympus Construction Systems, LLC. has existed for millenia. The lessons learned over those many long years highlighted the crucial importance of efficienct logistics for construction management. Logistics in construction management is all about getting people and resources where they need to go at precisely the right time. Whether on-site, in storage, or in transit, construction industry logistics is about knowing where materials and resources are at every stage of the project.<br/><br/>Several crucial case studies of failed construction projects due to poor logistics were highligted in several training modules in the archive. We can use these to improve our own construction efforts. 
TIProjectTemplate.displayName.Project_VaultRewardUnderhiveOlympusOriginalHiveModulesArchive=OCS Construction Blueprint Archive
TIProjectTemplate.summary.Project_VaultRewardUnderhiveOlympusOriginalHiveModulesArchive=This data-archive was retrieved from an ancient vault deep in the Underhive of a Terran Hive city.
TIProjectTemplate.description.Project_VaultRewardUnderhiveOlympusOriginalHiveModulesArchive=This datavault is truly massive in scale, containing every blueprint that OCS ever designed, prototpyed, or built. Unfortunatly, many of the designs have been flagged as obsolete, suffered data-corruption, or are encrypted beyond our capacity to decipher. Those that are readable, however, detail every material used, manufacturing process, tolerances, and construction method from indiviual power plant componenets to full scale arcologies. With a great deal of research, we will be able to match modules currently in use in hive cities to their original blueprints and restore them accordingly; provided, of course, that they are Olympus Construction Systems products. Considering the scale, longevity, and influence of OCS over the millenia, that is extremely likely.
TIProjectTemplate.displayName.Project_VaultRewardUnderhiveOlympusOriginalHiveModulesArchiveResearchOriginalHiveSkeleton=Restored Hive Skeleton
TIProjectTemplate.summary.Project_VaultRewardUnderhiveOlympusOriginalHiveModulesArchiveResearchOriginalHiveSkeleton=Further understanding of the original OCS templates will allow us to restore the foundations, internal structures, and integrity fields to peak condition
TIProjectTemplate.description.Project_VaultRewardUnderhiveOlympusOriginalHiveModulesArchiveResearchOriginalHiveSkeleton="The foundations of any arcology must be grounded in long-term thinking, for the inhabitants will be dependant on the initial design decisions of the founders for many years to come. I won't accept anything less than perfection!"<br/>-Chief Architect Lori Sheridan, Excerpt from OCS "Thessaloniki Arcology" Design Meeting Minutes<br/><br/>Such is the case for the hive cities built on the foundations of OCS arcologies. With the templates and the integrity field configurations we have analzed, restoration of the internal structures of the hives under out control will become possible. 
TIProjectTemplate.displayName.Project_VaultRewardUnderhiveOlympusOriginalHiveModulesArchiveResearchOriginalHiveMine=Restored Hive Recycling Complexes
TIProjectTemplate.summary.Project_VaultRewardUnderhiveOlympusOriginalHiveModulesArchiveResearchOriginalHiveMine=Further understanding of the original OCS templates will allow us to restore Hive recycling complexes to peak condition
TIProjectTemplate.description.Project_VaultRewardUnderhiveOlympusOriginalHiveModulesArchiveResearchOriginalHiveMine="The population density of any large-scale arcology requires the recycling of elements that humans require to live: water, air, food, and heat. Water can be filtered and purified from waste products. Air can be recycled by reacting with carbon dioxide and hydrogen, producing water and methane.  Electrolysis of water can produce oxygen and hydrogen. Heat managment can be done by transferring waste heat from industrial processes and distributing it evenly amongs habitable areas. Sustainable food can be grown from a variety of sources, including fungi, hydroponics, and algae. All these processes can make living in an arcology more sustainable."<br/>-Lifecycle Adept Tomos O'Neill, Excerpt from OCS "Thessaloniki Arcology" Design Meeting Minutes<br/><br/>These were the guiding priciples of OCS when desiging their arcologies, and we can adapt their techniques to the reality of living in a hive city today.
TIProjectTemplate.displayName.Project_VaultRewardUnderhiveOlympusOriginalHiveModulesArchiveResearchOriginalFusionReactor=Restored Hive Fusion Reactors 
TIProjectTemplate.summary.Project_VaultRewardUnderhiveOlympusOriginalHiveModulesArchiveResearchOriginalFusionReactor=Further understanding of the original OCS templates will allow us to restore Hive fusion reactors to peak condition
TIProjectTemplate.description.Project_VaultRewardUnderhiveOlympusOriginalHiveModulesArchiveResearchOriginalFusionReactor="Fusion processes require fuel and a confined environment with sufficient temperature, pressure, and confinement time to create a plasma in which fusion can occur. Failure to properly configure and monitor such variables can lead to lower reactor output as well as catastrophic containment breaches. Don't tell me that you are going to skip saftey protocols just becasue it will cut costs!"<br/>-Chief Systems Engineer Eduard Guerrero, Excerpt from OCS "Thessaloniki Arcology" Design Meeting Minutes<br/><br/>Discovery of the original manufacturer's specifications, blueprints, and construction methods will allow restoration of decayed and jury-rigged hive fusion reactors to their orginal power output.
TIProjectTemplate.displayName.Project_VaultRewardUnderhiveOlympusOriginalHiveModulesArchiveResearchOriginalHiveHabBlock=Restored Hive Hab-Blocks
TIProjectTemplate.summary.Project_VaultRewardUnderhiveOlympusOriginalHiveModulesArchiveResearchOriginalHiveHabBlock=Further understanding of the original OCS templates will allow us to restore Hive Hab-Blocks to peak condition
TIProjectTemplate.description.Project_VaultRewardUnderhiveOlympusOriginalHiveModulesArchiveResearchOriginalHiveHabBlock="The importance of habitation areas that provide a safe and comfortable living space for colonists is not to be underestimated. The ability for a worker to come home to a well-lit, safe place to rest is essential to maintain work eficeincy and productivity. We can try to pack them in like sardines, but that is an unsustainable model for any long-term project."<br/>-Senior Civil Designer Cassius Traynor, Excerpt from OCS "Thessaloniki Arcology" Design Meeting Minutes<br/><br/>


TIProjectTemplate.displayName.Project_VaultRewardUnderhiveOlympusSTCFragment01=STC Fragment OCS-Alpha-001
TIProjectTemplate.summary.Project_VaultRewardUnderhiveOlympusSTCFragment01=This heavily encrypted datavault contains portions of OCS's contribution to the STC project
TIProjectTemplate.description.Project_VaultRewardUnderhiveOlympusSTCFragment01=This fragment of an STC datavault is heavilly encrypted, and judging by the ident-codes on the outer matrix, will become only become decipherable in combination with other STC fragments. We are able to decipher this header string, however:<br/><br/> 10101111.itan....shield.....lance...batteries.....purifier...100010001

TIProjectTemplate.displayName.Project_RecruitmentCouncilorRetinueBarbarian=Recruit from the Techno-Barbarian Tribes
TIProjectTemplate.summary.Project_RecruitmentCouncilorRetinueBarbarian=Seek hardened warriors from the local unconsolidated tribes four your retinue
TIProjectTemplate.description.Project_RecruitmentCouncilorRetinueBarbarian=Techno-barbarians is the name given to the warriors who battled over the ruins of Terra during the Age of Strife. They formed the troops of the warlords who dominated Terra during the period, and were equipped with a primitive form of powered armor which would become the basis for the developments of Space Marine armor. These warriors will serve in your retinue.

TIProjectTemplate.displayName.Project_OrganizationImperialBiotechnicalDivision=Peer Review the Imperial Biotechnical Division
TIProjectTemplate.summary.Project_OrganizationImperialBiotechnicalDivision=It has existed in a loose formation for some time, but now is the time to reorganize, and possibly vote in a new Director.
TIProjectTemplate.description.Project_OrganizationImperialBiotechnicalDivision=The Biotechnical Division is an organization of geneticists of the Emperor's own inner research cadres. Formed on Terra, the division is charged with developing the very first Space Marines. Their first director has been chosen by the Emperor Himself, should Amar Astarte choose to accept it.
TIProjectTemplate.displayName.Project_OrganizationImperialEstateImperium=Audit the Estate Imperium
TIProjectTemplate.summary.Project_OrganizationImperialEstateImperium=Ensure the account records balance correctly, and if not, replace the Chancellor
TIProjectTemplate.description.Project_OrganizationImperialEstateImperium=The Estate Imperium is a division of the Administratum, described as "the million-strong records office of the Administratum". Its purpose is to keep and furnish records of Imperial organizations. The Estate Imperium is also one of the overseers of the vast Departmento Munitorum. The Chancellor of the Estate Imperium is the highest official within the Estate Imperium. He also has the duty of overseeing the Departmento Munitorum's Office of the Imperial Pursary.
TIProjectTemplate.displayName.Project_OrganizationImperialAdministratum=Review the Adeptus Administratum
TIProjectTemplate.summary.Project_OrganizationImperialAdministratum=Ensure all records are in order, otherwise replace the Master of the Administratum
TIProjectTemplate.description.Project_OrganizationImperialAdministratum=The Adeptus Administratum is the administrative and bureaucratic division of the Adeptus Terra, consisting of untold numbers of clerks, scribes and administrative staff constantly working to manage the Imperium at every level, from assembling war fleets to levying taxes. The Master of the Administratum is the title of the head of the Administratum. The holder of this prestigious rank holds a position on the High Lords of Terra. Among the High Lords this rank is the most powerful. The Master of the Administratum is also one of the the key directors of the Departmento Munitorum.
TIProjectTemplate.displayName.Project_OrganizationImperialAdeptusArbites=Reform the Adeptus Arbites
TIProjectTemplate.summary.Project_OrganizationImperialAdeptusArbites=Review all polices and procedures, and if necessary, appint an new Grand Provost Marshal
TIProjectTemplate.description.Project_OrganizationImperialAdeptusArbites=The Adeptus Arbites are the police force of the Adeptus Terra, devoted to enforcing Imperial law throughout the entire Imperium. The Grand Provost Marshal is the commander of the Adeptus Arbites. A permanent member of the High Lords of Terra, the Grand Provost Marshal represents the Emperor's Law to the rest of the High Lords and is a key source of legal advice.
TIProjectTemplate.displayName.Project_OrganizationImperialArmy=Reorganize the Imperial Army
TIProjectTemplate.summary.Project_OrganizationImperialArmy=Ensure all drills and excercises are up to date, otherwise promote a new Lord Commander Militant
TIProjectTemplate.description.Project_OrganizationImperialArmy=The Departmento Munitorum (or Munitorium) is a department of the Administratum devoted to the general administration, supply and command of the Imperial Army. The Munitorum has ultimate responsibility for the raising of new regiments, training of troops, provision of equipment and supplies, and transportation of troops and equipment to and from theatres of war. It is primarily a logistical organisation, like the Administratum, but while the Administratum deals with civilian logistics, the Munitorum deals with the logistics of war. The Lord Commander Militant is the highest ranked figure within the Imperial Army and the Departmento Munitorum and represents the Army on the High Lords of Terra.

TIProjectTemplate.displayName.Project_DesignTemplateShipSkylanceGunship=Template: Skylance Gunship
TIProjectTemplate.summary.Project_DesignTemplateShipSkylanceGunship=These are the secrets of constructing the Skylance Gunship, an early assault transport.
TIProjectTemplate.description.Project_DesignTemplateShipSkylanceGunship=The Skylance Gunship, also known as the Skylance Drop-ship, was a type of gunship used during the later days of the Unification Wars on Terra by the forces of the Emperor. The Skylance was used by the Thunder Warriors and also by the early Legiones Astartes. Designed to rapidly insert assault troops in hostile environments, it also has a configuration for transporting important personnel. Its primary limitation is its low internal fuel capacity, which can be mitigated somewhat by external fuel tanks for long-range operations.


