TIBatteryTemplate.displayName.SupercapaciterBattery=Supercapacitor Battery
TIBatteryTemplate.description.SupercapaciterBattery=An advanced lightweight battery with zero electrical resistance and a extremely rapid recharge rate.  
TIBatteryTemplate.displayName.BatteryTemplateSkylance=Skylance Internal Capacitor
TIBatteryTemplate.description.BatteryTemplateSkylance=Assaulting an enemy position under fire requires defending against enemy missiles and projectiles, so this capacitor contains sufficient energy to feed the point defence systems.

TIDriveTemplate.displayName.PlasmaticDrivex1=Plasmatic Wave Drive x1
TIDriveTemplate.description.PlasmaticDrivex1=This ancient drive system uses internally-generated magnetic fields to eject plasma at high speeds from the drive's engine housings. 
TIDriveTemplate.displayName.PlasmaticDrivex2=Plasmatic Wave Drive x2
TIDriveTemplate.displayName.PlasmaticDrivex3=Plasmatic Wave Drive x3
TIDriveTemplate.displayName.PlasmaticDrivex4=Plasmatic Wave Drive x4
TIDriveTemplate.displayName.PlasmaticDrivex5=Plasmatic Wave Drive x5
TIDriveTemplate.displayName.PlasmaticDrivex6=Plasmatic Wave Drive x6
TIDriveTemplate.displayName.DriveTemplateSkylance=Skylance MultiFuel Engine
TIDriveTemplate.description.DriveTemplateSkylance=The Skylance is capable of atmospheric flight, as well as brief jaunts into the void. Its engine system can accept various formulations of promethium as its fuel source.

TIPowerPlantTemplate.displayName.MirroredCellFusionReactorI=Mirrored Fusion Reactor I
TIPowerPlantTemplate.description.MirroredCellFusionReactorI=A linear fusion reactor that uses magnetic mirrors to contain and direct plasma.
TIPowerPlantTemplate.displayName.MirroredCellFusionReactorII=Mirrored Fusion Reactor II
TIPowerPlantTemplate.description.MirroredCellFusionReactorII=A linear fusion reactor that uses magnetic mirrors to contain and direct plasma. This version contains improved mirror microcorrectional algorithms.
TIPowerPlantTemplate.displayName.MirroredCellFusionReactorIII=Mirrored Fusion Reactor III
TIPowerPlantTemplate.description.MirroredCellFusionReactorIII=A linear fusion reactor that uses magnetic mirrors to contain and direct plasma. This version contains improved mirror microcorrectional algorithms and superior materials.
TIPowerPlantTemplate.displayName.PowerPlantTemplateSkylance=Skylance Minifusor Reactor
TIPowerPlantTemplate.description.PowerPlantTemplateSkylance=The power for the Skylance's internal sytems is provided by electro-confined fusion energies. 

TIRadiatorTemplate.displayName.VoidRadiator=Void Radiator
TIRadiatorTemplate.description.VoidRadiator=Unknown materials swiftly gather excess energy and expel it into space, allowing for the efficient disposal of waste heat.
TIRadiatorTemplate.displayName.RadiatorTemplateSkylance=Skylance Venting Subsystem
TIRadiatorTemplate.description.RadiatorTemplateSkylance=Heat managment for the Skylance is almost an afterthought, as one is not worried about overheating from the point defence lasers firing, but rather taking damage from enemmy munitions. There is a rudimentary venting system, however.

TIHeatSinkTemplate.displayName.ThermalDissipatorSink=Thermal Dissipator
TIHeatSinkTemplate.description.ThermalDissipatorSink=Unknown materials swiftly gather excess energy, providing unparalleled capacity to store heat.
TIHeatSinkTemplate.displayName.HeavyThermalDissipatorSink=Heavy Thermal Dissipator
TIHeatSinkTemplate.description.HeavyThermalDissipatorSink=Unknown materials swiftly gather excess energy, providing unparalleled capacity to store heat. This is a larger storage configuration.
TIHeatSinkTemplate.displayName.HeatSinkTemplateSkylance=Skylance Life Sustainment System
TIHeatSinkTemplate.description.HeatSinkTemplateSkylance=These consist of the air scrubbers, temperature contols, and gravatic systems to allow crew to exist within the vehicle. They can be turned off for additional stealth capabilities if all occupants are in void-sealed armors.

TIShipArmorTemplate.displayName.MirroredArmor=Mirrored Armor
TIShipArmorTemplate.description.MirroredArmor=Unknown materials reflect photonic energy, providing resistance to most laser weaponry.
TIShipArmorTemplate.displayName.ShipArmorTemplateSkylance=Skylance Ceramite Armor
TIShipArmorTemplate.description.ShipArmorTemplateSkylance=Ceramite is a kind of bonded ceramic armour, especially tough, but light. Repairs are made by setting new layers of ceramite over existing ones. Unlike metal, Ceramite doesn’t rupture or dent on impact and it takes a projectile of considerable power and high calibre to break through it. It also posesses a high thermal tolerance, making it sutable for hybrid atmospheric/voidcraft.

TIUtilityModuleTemplate.displayName.UtilityModuleInternalsArcheotechRedundancy=Internals:Archeotech Redundancies
TIUtilityModuleTemplate.description.UtilityModuleInternalsArcheotechRedundancy=This ship contains many archeotech backups and failsafes that helps prevent internal damage from affecting ship functions. It appears that whoever designed this aspect of the ship focused on redundancies over efficiency, as some of the backup systems occasionally interfere with engine performance.
TIUtilityModuleTemplate.displayName.UtilityModuleTemplateSkylanceInternals=Internals: Skylance Assault Gunship
TIUtilityModuleTemplate.description.UtilityModuleTemplateSkylanceInternals=As an assault gunship dedicated to landing forces to hostile landing zones, the Skylance is a rather spartan and functional ship. There is little manner of decoration or upholstery, save that needed for troops in transit or the piolot's compartment. All important switches and supply caches are labeled in crisp, militaristic language, with dire warnings if safety protocols are not followed. Older gunships may contain war trophys from battles fought, battle scars from tense landings or evactuations, and the pilot's seat my contain certain embellishments detailing certain daring exploits during the craft's history. 
TIUtilityModuleTemplate.displayName.UtilityModuleTemplateSkylanceMarinesThunderWarriors=Marines: Thunder Warrior Platoon
TIUtilityModuleTemplate.description.UtilityModuleTemplateSkylanceMarinesThunderWarriors=A platoon of Thunder warriors and associated equipment, ready to visit extreme violence upon their foes.
TIUtilityModuleTemplate.displayName.UtilityModuleTemplateSkylanceWingFuelPods=Externals: Skylance Fuel Pods
TIUtilityModuleTemplate.description.UtilityModuleTemplateSkylanceWingFuelPods=These are fuel pods that contain additional propellant for long-term operations

TILaserWeaponTemplate.displayName.LaserWeaponTemplateSkyLancePointDefenseLaserTurret=Skylance PD Laser Turret
TILaserWeaponTemplate.description.LaserWeaponTemplateSkyLancePointDefenseLaserTurret=A very short-range infrared laser capable of shooting down incoming projectiles.

TIGunTemplate.displayName.GunTemplateSkylance50mmAutocannon=Skylance Twin-linked Autocannon
TIGunTemplate.description.GunTemplateSkylance50mmAutocannon=Rapid-fire autocannon that is primarily useful in clearing a ladning zone of enemy infantry but can also be used in a defensive role.

TIShipHullTemplate.displayName.ShipHullEscortImperialSkylance=Skylance Gunship
TIShipHullTemplate.abbr.ShipHullEscortImperialSkylance=SLG

TISpaceShipTemplate.displayName.SpaceShipTemplateImperialSkylanceGunship=Assault



TIObjectiveTemplate.displayName.HumanGeneralTerra=Bring Terra's Tribes and Nations Under Your Control
TIObjectiveTemplate.description.HumanGeneralTerra=Amid the uncertainty about the cessation of the warp storms and xeno incursions, we have an opportunity to establish ourselves as the superme global leader. We must bring all of Terra's warring polities and tribes under our dominion.<br/><br/>To that end, our first priority should be to send our councilors to gain control points in nations with strong economies, militaries and research and space programs, and initiating public campaigns where necessary to sway the public to our cause.<br/><br/>Much of Terras's economy is wasted on "spoils" — people enriching themselves at others' expense; with sufficient control, we can reorient those nations to serve more productive ends.<br/><br/>If diplomacy will not suffice, we must crush all resistance under the might of our armies.
TIObjectiveTemplate.solution.HumanGeneralTerra=Have your councilors conduct Unrest missions to gain Control Points in Earth's nations. Employ armies to invade enemy nations and impose regimes allied to our cause. Set the priorities of those nations to develop space and research programs, improve stability and economic output, and to field defenses against our rivals. 

TIObjectiveTemplate.displayName.HumanGeneralArcheotech=Recover Lost Technologies and Archeotech
TIObjectiveTemplate.description.HumanGeneralArcheotech=Much of the Glory that was Humanity in the Dark Age of Technology has been lost, but some still remains. Search for lost relics and technologies among abandoned research stations, the decaying shipyards of Jupiter and Saturn, mining colonies amidst the asteroid belt, and upon the ruined surface of Terra. These dark recesses of the Sol system may be infested with rouge AI, mutants, pirates, or worse; however, successful expeditions may bring back much lost knowledge and powerful artifacts. With these recovered relics of a brighter age, we may wield their power and thus secure our future. 
TIObjectiveTemplate.solution.HumanGeneralArcheotech=Assign a Councilor to conduct a "Search for Archeotech" mission on a hab that contains a Vault Module (this will be indicated in the tooltip of the module itself). They must then overcome a series of challenges, encounters, and obstacles that depend on strong attributes and a variety of traits in order to succeed. The rewards, as well as the challenges, depend on the module in question. It is advised to equip your councilor with various augments and orgs before embarking upon such expeditions, as nearly all vaults contain situations that may lead to their death if they are not properly equipped.

TIObjectiveTemplate.displayName.HumanGeneralInnerCircle=Build the Inner Circle
TIObjectiveTemplate.description.HumanGeneralInnerCircle=Our councilors will form the backbone of our efforts on Terra and beyond. We must recruit a diverse, influential and loyal group of supporters to accomplish missions across the Sol system. 
TIObjectiveTemplate.solution.HumanGeneralInnerCircle=Spend Influence to recruit councilors with attributes and missions that best advance our cause. Acquire orgs that improve their capabilities. Equip them with the best tools, weapons, and armor for them to survive the cruel and uncaring universe.


